# Conn, Gould and Toint, Chapter 3: Basic Analysis and Optimality Conditions

Chapter 3 of [conn2000trust] gives the analysis that the convergence theory uses. Section 3.1 proves
the mean-value and Taylor formulas and the support identity (3.1.4) of the Clarke directional
derivative. Section 3.2 proves the first- and second-order optimality conditions for unconstrained,
constrained, convex and nonsmooth problems, and the continuity of parametric minima. Section 3.3
defines the Q- and R-rates of convergence and proves the convergence of Newton's method.

